  "alt": "Binary quantization stores each dimension in one bit instead of 32: every float32 value collapses to 1 if it is positive and 0 otherwise, a 32-fold cut in memory that also replaces floating-point dot products with XOR-based Hamming distance.",
  "caption": "Keeping only the sign of each value cuts memory 32×, at the cost of some recall.",
